<!-- this exercise was written by Chrissy Safranski as part of the PROTEUS grant-->

<setup>
  <boolean name="cc11">1 subset $cc1.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc12">2 subset $cc1.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc13">3 subset $cc1.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc14">4 subset $cc1.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc15">5 subset $cc1.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc16">6 subset $cc1.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc21">1 subset $cc2.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc22">2 subset $cc2.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc23">3 subset $cc2.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc24">4 subset $cc2.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc25">5 subset $cc2.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc26">6 subset $cc2.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc31">1 subset $cc3.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc32">2 subset $cc3.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc33">3 subset $cc3.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc34">4 subset $cc3.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc35">5 subset $cc3.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc36">6 subset $cc3.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc41">1 subset $cc4.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc42">2 subset $cc4.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc43">3 subset $cc4.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc44">4 subset $cc4.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc45">5 subset $cc4.selectedIndices</boolean>
  <boolean name="cc46">6 subset $cc4.selectedIndices</boolean>
</setup>
<p>
  Below are four conditions on the sign of the first or second derivative, along with six behaviors of the function or the first derivative.  Select which behavior(s) corresponds to which condition.  </p>
<p>
  Every behavior should be selected exactly once. To help with this, once a behavior has been selected it will disappear from the other menus; the behavior will reappear in all the menus if it is unselected.  Since there are four conditions on derivative signs and six function behaviors, at least one of the four sign conditions will have more than one behavior associated with it.
</p>
<ol marker="a.">
  <li>
    <p>
      When <m>f'(x) \gt 0</m>, it means that <choiceInput name="cc1" selectMultiple><shortDescription>function and derivative behaviors</shortDescription><choice hide="$cc21 or $cc31 or $cc41"><m>f(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc22 or $cc32 or $cc42"><m>f(x)</m> is decreasing</choice><choice hide="$cc23 or $cc33 or $cc43"><m>f(x)</m> is concave up</choice><choice hide="$cc24 or $cc34 or $cc44"><m>f(x)</m> is concave down</choice><choice hide="$cc25 or $cc35 or $cc45"><m>f'(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc26 or $cc36 or $cc46"><m>f'(x)</m> is decreasing</choice></choiceInput>
    </p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>
      When <m>f'(x) \lt 0</m>, it means that <choiceInput name="cc2" selectMultiple><shortDescription>function and derivative behaviors</shortDescription><choice hide="$cc11 or $cc31 or $cc41"><m>f(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc12 or $cc32 or $cc42"><m>f(x)</m> is decreasing</choice><choice hide="$cc13 or $cc33 or $cc43"><m>f(x)</m> is concave up</choice><choice hide="$cc14 or $cc34 or $cc44"><m>f(x)</m> is concave down</choice><choice hide="$cc15 or $cc35 or $cc45"><m>f'(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc16 or $cc36 or $cc46"><m>f'(x)</m> is decreasing</choice></choiceInput>
    </p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>
      When <m>f''(x) \gt 0</m>, it means that <choiceInput name="cc3" selectMultiple><shortDescription>function and derivative behaviors</shortDescription><choice hide="$cc11 or $cc21 or $cc41"><m>f(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc12 or $cc22 or $cc42"><m>f(x)</m> is decreasing</choice><choice hide="$cc13 or $cc23 or $cc43"><m>f(x)</m> is concave up</choice><choice hide="$cc14 or $cc24 or $cc44"><m>f(x)</m> is concave down</choice><choice hide="$cc15 or $cc25 or $cc45"><m>f'(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc16 or $cc26 or $cc46"><m>f'(x)</m> is decreasing</choice></choiceInput>
    </p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>
      When <m>f''(x) \lt 0</m>, it means that <choiceInput name="cc4" selectMultiple><shortDescription>function and derivative behaviors</shortDescription><choice hide="$cc11 or $cc21 or $cc31"><m>f(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc12 or $cc22 or $cc32"><m>f(x)</m> is decreasing</choice><choice hide="$cc13 or $cc23 or $cc33"><m>f(x)</m> is concave up</choice><choice hide="$cc14 or $cc24 or $cc34"><m>f(x)</m> is concave down</choice><choice hide="$cc15 or $cc25 or $cc35"><m>f'(x)</m> is increasing</choice><choice hide="$cc16 or $cc26 or $cc36"><m>f'(x)</m> is decreasing</choice></choiceInput>
    </p>
  </li>
</ol>
<answer><award><when>$cc1.selectedIndex=1 and $cc2.selectedIndex=2 and $cc3.selectedIndices=<mathList>3,5</mathList> and $cc4.selectedIndices=<mathList>4,6</mathList></when></award></answer>